{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they complained.</b> At the waters of Marah they complained against Moses alone, for he alone had led them out, and not all Israel complained but only some of them; therefore it is written, \"and the people complained\" (above, 15:24). But now, in the wilderness of Sin, \"all the congregation of Israel complained against Moses and against Aaron,\" for both of them had brought them out. At Marah they grumbled about the water; now they grumble about meat and bread, for they had already consumed most of their flocks, and in a great multitude like theirs they would not find bread to purchase except at a high price, for it was thirty days since the day they came out."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:58.438389103Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}